<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhu Ying</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhu Ying was an official of Eastern Wu who travelled with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kang-tai">Kang Tai</a> on an embassy sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-quan">Sun Quan</a> to Funan, in mainland South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, in the mid-3rd century. He wrote an account of the country and its neighbours, now lost but cited in later Chinese works, which with Kang Tai's report forms the oldest Chinese description of Funan.</p></div>
